 "source": "# Written the way a person writes YAML and prettier does not. Every other\n# file in this corpus probes what prettier *breaks*; this one probes what\n# it *rewrites*. Nothing here is about line width -- each rewrite happens\n# at every width.\n\n# Spacing around `:`, which people pad by hand and prettier collapses.\nname:    demo\nversion:  \"0.1.0\"\nenabled:  true\n\n# Padding inside flow brackets, and spacing around the commas.\npadded: [ 1 , 2 , 3 ]\ntight: [1,2,3]\n# Flow mappings are the mirror image: prettier pads the braces out.\ncompact: {x: 1,y: 2}\nhalf: { x: 1,y: 2 }\n\n# Sequence dashes flush with the key, which YAML allows and prettier indents.\nroot:\n- first\n- second\nnested:\n  list:\n  - one\n  - two\n\n# A nested sequence written with the dash on its own line; prettier\n# collapses it to the compact `- - item` form.\nflags:\n  - one\n  -\n    - nested-a\n    - nested-b\n\n# Runs of spaces (and a tab) before a trailing comment.\nport: 8080          # many spaces before this one\nhost: localhost\t# a tab before this one\n\n# A source trailing comma on a flat flow sequence is dropped.\ntrailing: [1, 2, 3,]\n\n# Explicit `?` keys; prettier writes the implicit form. Named tree is unchanged.\n? explicit\n: value\n\n\n\n# Three or more blank lines above; prettier caps a run at one.\nreplicas: 2\n",
